{
  "name": "session.view",
  "description": "Get the session's windows, their layouts, and their blocks in one snapshot.",
  "invoke": {
    "method": "session.view"
  },
  "input_schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "session_id": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The session to act on."
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "session_id"
    ],
    "additionalProperties": false
  },
  "output_schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "active_window_id": {
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ],
        "description": "The window the session shows. Left out when the session has no windows."
      },
      "label": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "The session's label."
      },
      "revision": {
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "The view's revision. A larger revision is a newer view of the session, even across a server restart. It goes up by one with each change, and jumps ahead when a restarted server restores the session.",
        "minimum": 0
      },
      "session_id": {
        "type": [
          "string",
          "null"
        ],
        "description": "The session's ID."
      },
      "windows": {
        "type": [
          "null",
          "array"
        ],
        "items": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "focused_block_id": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ],
              "description": "The window's focused block, which receives typing while the window is active. Left out if the window has none."
            },
            "label": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The window's label."
            },
            "layers": {
              "type": [
                "null",
                "array"
              ],
              "items": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "blocks": {
                    "type": [
                      "null",
                      "array"
                    ],
                    "items": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "properties": {
                        "block_id": {
                          "type": [
                            "string",
                            "null"
                          ],
                          "description": "The block's ID."
                        },
                        "creator_name": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "description": "The creator that made the block, such as com.superlogical.terminal."
                        },
                        "flavor": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "description": "The flavor the block was made from, such as com.superlogical.terminal.shell."
                        },
                        "host_id": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "description": "Identifies the machine and account the block runs as. If it equals your local server's host_id, the block sees the same files you do. Otherwise treat the block as remote."
                        },
                        "label": {
                          "type": "string",
                          "description": "The block's label."
                        },
                        "owner": {
                          "type": [
                            "string",
                            "null"
                          ],
                          "description": "The client that owns the block. Left out when the block has no owner."
                        }
                      },
                      "required": [
                        "block_id"
                      ],
                      "additionalProperties": false
                    },
                    "description": "The blocks in the layer, in layout order. The layout field says where each one sits."
                  },
                  "bounds": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "number"
                    },
                    "description": "Where the layer sits, as [x, y, w, h] fractions of the window's width and height.",
                    "minItems": 4,
                    "maxItems": 4
                  },
                  "kind": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "How the layer is placed: 'tiled' for the layer that fills the window, or 'floating' for a floating layer. Draw a kind you don't know as 'floating'."
                  },
                  "layer_id": {
                    "type": [
                      "string",
                      "null"
                    ],
                    "description": "The layer's ID."
                  },
                  "layout": {
                    "type": [
                      "object",
                      "null"
                    ],
                    "properties": {
                      "block_id": {
                        "type": [
                          "string",
                          "null"
                        ],
                        "description": "The block at this node. Set only when split isn't."
                      },
                      "rect": {
                        "type": "array",
                        "items": {
                          "type": "number"
                        },
                        "description": "Where this node sits, as [x, y, w, h] fractions of the window's width and height.",
                        "minItems": 4,
                        "maxItems": 4
                      },
                      "split": {
                        "type": [
                          "object",
                          "null"
                        ],
                        "properties": {
                          "after": {
                            "$ref": "#view-layout-node",
                            "description": "The node on the right or bottom."
                          },
                          "before": {
                            "$ref": "#view-layout-node",
                            "description": "The node on the left or top."
                          },
                          "direction": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "How the space is divided: 'horizontal' puts before on the left and after on the right, and 'vertical' puts before above after. Draw a direction you don't know as 'horizontal'.",
                            "enum": [
                              "horizontal",
                              "vertical"
                            ]
                          },
                          "ratio": {
                            "type": "number",
                            "description": "The fraction of the space that before gets, between 0 and 1."
                          },
                          "split_id": {
                            "type": [
                              "string",
                              "null"
                            ],
                            "description": "The split's ID. It stays the same while the split exists, so you can match splits across views."
                          }
                        },
                        "description": "How this node divides in two. Set only when block_id isn't.",
                        "required": [
                          "split_id",
                          "direction",
                          "ratio",
                          "before",
                          "after"
                        ]
                      }
                    },
                    "$anchor": "view-layout-node",
                    "description": "How the layer divides its space between blocks, as a tree of splits. Null when the layer is empty.",
                    "required": [
                      "rect"
                    ]
                  },
                  "state": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "How the layer is presented: 'minimized' means don't draw it, though its blocks keep running, and only a floating layer can be minimized. Left out for a normal layer. Draw a state you don't know as normal."
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "layer_id",
                  "kind",
                  "bounds",
                  "layout",
                  "blocks"
                ],
                "additionalProperties": false
              },
              "description": "The window's layers, from back to front. The first is the tiled layer, which holds the window's layout and fills the window."
            },
            "window_id": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ],
              "description": "The window's ID."
            },
            "zoomed_block_id": {
              "type": [
                "string",
                "null"
              ],
              "description": "The block zoomed to fill the window, if any. Layouts keep their normal sizes, so draw this block over the whole window."
            }
          },
          "required": [
            "window_id",
            "layers"
          ],
          "additionalProperties": false
        },
        "description": "The session's windows, in order. Rex.app shows them as tabs in this order."
      }
    },
    "required": [
      "revision",
      "session_id"
    ],
    "additionalProperties": false
  },
  "request_example": "{\n  \"session_id\": \"session:<uuid>\"\n}",
  "response_example": "{\n  \"revision\": 7,\n  \"session_id\": \"session:<uuid>\",\n  \"label\": \"work\",\n  \"active_window_id\": \"window:<uuid>\",\n  \"windows\": [\n    {\n      \"window_id\": \"window:<uuid>\",\n      \"label\": \"editor\",\n      \"focused_block_id\": \"block:01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcde1\",\n      \"layers\": [\n        {\n          \"layer_id\": \"layer:<uuid>\",\n          \"kind\": \"tiled\",\n          \"bounds\": [0, 0, 1, 1],\n          \"layout\": {\n            \"rect\": [0, 0, 1, 1],\n            \"split\": {\n              \"split_id\": \"split:<uuid>\",\n              \"direction\": \"horizontal\",\n              \"ratio\": 0.5,\n              \"before\": {\n                \"rect\": [0, 0, 0.5, 1],\n                \"block_id\": \"block:01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcde1\"\n              },\n              \"after\": {\n                \"rect\": [0.5, 0, 0.5, 1],\n                \"block_id\": \"block:01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcde2\"\n              }\n            }\n          },\n          \"blocks\": [\n            {\n              \"block_id\": \"block:01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcde1\",\n              \"label\": \"shell\",\n              \"creator_name\": \"com.superlogical.terminal\",\n              \"flavor\": \"com.superlogical.terminal.shell\",\n              \"host_id\": \"0e9d6c1f-4a3b-4a52-9c85-2f6d3f6f2f10\",\n              \"owner\": \"client:<uuid>\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"block_id\": \"block:01234567-89ab-cdef-0123-456789abcde2\",\n              \"label\": \"logs\",\n              \"creator_name\": \"com.superlogical.terminal\",\n              \"flavor\": \"com.superlogical.terminal.shell\",\n              \"host_id\": \"0e9d6c1f-4a3b-4a52-9c85-2f6d3f6f2f10\",\n              \"owner\": \"client:<uuid>\"\n            }\n          ]\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
  "validation_notes": [
    "`revision` starts at zero for a new session and goes up by one each time the view changes. Compare revisions only within one session, and keep the view with the highest revision.",
    "A `session_view_changed` event carries only the new revision, not the view. These events can arrive out of revision order, so call `session.view` only when an event's revision is higher than the one in the view you hold.",
    "`window_created`, `window_closed`, `window_label_changed`, `active_window_changed`, and `session_label_changed` arrive before the `session_view_changed` event for the same change.",
    "The view holds only blocks that are in a window. `session.list_blocks` also lists detached blocks.",
    "The view describes structure, not content. To read what a block shows, call one of its own methods, such as `com.superlogical.terminal.format`."
  ]
}
